
// On the left side of this rule the 'caps:' prefix is a UI grouping convention,
// not a file name.
//
// The right side 'capslock_shift' is the file's name in the ../symbols folder
// and 'shift_modifier' is the section in that file.  The file is deliberately
// not called 'capslock' -- see the comment at the top of it for why that would
// break every other caps:* option.
! option = symbols
caps:shift_modifier = +capslock_shift(shift_modifier)

// Since the rules reader stops searching file paths at the first one found,
// we explicitly need to import the system rules.
//
// Keeping the include last also means our symbols are applied before all stock
// ones, so any stock option that claims <CAPS> too (lv3:caps_switch,
// grp:caps_toggle, ...) silently overrides caps:shift_modifier, whatever order
// the options are listed in.  That is the safer direction to fail in, but it is
// no substitute for a UI that stops the two from being selected together.
! include %S/evdev
